OL,3,GNEWSALabour council leader ousted after
OL,4,Afour months
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Labour leader of Luton Borough
OL,7,FCouncil has lost a no-confidence vote
OL,8,Fafter being in the role less than four
OL,9,Fmonths.
OL,11,FTahmina Saleem was appointed in May to
OL,12,Freplace long-serving Hazel Simmons, but
OL,13,Fhas faced a leadership challenge which
OL,14,Fputs Liberal Democrat Amjid Ali in
OL,15,Fcharge of a coalition-led authority.
OL,17,FAli said: "I am honoured and humbled to
OL,18,Fbe given this opportunity and fully
OL,19,Frecognise the significant
OL,20,Fresponsibility that comes with it. Our
OL,21,Fabsolute commitment will be to the
OL,22,Fpeople of Luton."
OL,23,APub: 15-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
